      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_6_gk2.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Tom: Hello Linh! What programme or sport are you researching for English class?\nLinh: Hi Tom! I am presenting about Exploring Big Ben and London Landmarks related to London.\nTom: What is the most exciting aspect of this topic?\nLinh: Audiences and participants are fascinated by Big Ben clock tower and love riding double-decker bus.\nTom: How does it inspire young students?\nLinh: It encourages teamwork, expands knowledge of River Thames, and highlights British museum.\nTom: That is brilliant! I look forward to listening to your speech.",
      "clozeText": "Exploring exploring big ben and london landmarks provides valuable lessons for secondary school students. Whether situated in London or on international screens, this subject inspires teenagers with Big Ben clock tower. Many students find that riding double-decker bus helps them build self-confidence and (23) ________. However, experts advise viewers that they (24) ________ spend too many consecutive hours in front of screens. Instead, balancing television viewing with outdoor physical (25) ________ ensures good health. In addition, learning about River Thames broadens our awareness of the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, approaching entertainment with a smart mindset leads to a (27) ________ lifestyle.",
      "readingText": "Exploring Big Ben and London Landmarks has captured the enthusiastic interest of young audiences who appreciate London. Combining informative insights with engaging entertainment, it showcases Big Ben clock tower and provides deep perspectives on River Thames. Many teenagers report that participating in riding double-decker bus enhances their concentration, boosts physical endurance, and alleviates academic stress. Moreover, instructors and educators emphasize British museum as a core pillar of personal development and fair play. Whether practicing on sports grounds or exploring international landmarks, students acquire practical knowledge that transcends textbooks. Cultivating healthy habits through balanced sports and informative media prepares youths for success in modern society.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nExploring exploring big ben and london landmarks provides valuable lessons for secondary school students. Whether situated in London or on international screens, this subject inspires teenagers with Big Ben clock tower. Many students find that riding double-decker bus helps them build self-confidence and (23) ________. However, experts advise viewers that they (24) ________ spend too many consecutive hours in front of screens. Instead, balancing television viewing with outdoor physical (25) ________ ensures good health. In addition, learning about River Thames broadens our awareness of the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, approaching entertainment with a smart mindset leads to a (27) ________ lifestyle.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nExploring Big Ben and London Landmarks has captured the enthusiastic interest of young audiences who appreciate London. Combining informative insights with engaging entertainment, it showcases Big Ben clock tower and provides deep perspectives on River Thames. Many teenagers report that participating in riding double-decker bus enhances their concentration, boosts physical endurance, and alleviates academic stress. Moreover, instructors and educators emphasize British museum as a core pillar of personal development and fair play. Whether practicing on sports grounds or exploring international landmarks, students acquire practical knowledge that transcends textbooks. Cultivating healthy habits through balanced sports and informative media prepares youths for success in modern society.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Why you like it; Important features of London; What benefits it brings; How it helps your study.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, Exploring Big Ben and London Landmarks is an inspiring aspect of modern life. It connects us with London while promoting Big Ben clock tower. Engaging in riding double-decker bus helps students relieve academic stress and develop River Thames. Furthermore, respecting the spirit of British museum encourages discipline and fair play. I believe every student should embrace these healthy habits.",
