      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nExploring wildlife documentaries on national geographic provides valuable lessons for secondary school students. Whether situated in documentary channel or on international screens, this subject inspires teenagers with polar bears in Arctic. Many students find that taking nature notes helps them build self-confidence and (23) ________. However, experts advise viewers that they (24) ________ spend too many consecutive hours in front of screens. Instead, balancing television viewing with outdoor physical (25) ________ ensures good health. In addition, learning about ocean dolphins broadens our awareness of the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, approaching entertainment with a smart mindset leads to a (27) ________ lifestyle.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nWildlife Documentaries on National Geographic has captured the enthusiastic interest of young audiences who appreciate documentary channel. Combining informative insights with engaging entertainment, it showcases polar bears in Arctic and provides deep perspectives on ocean dolphins. Many teenagers report that participating in taking nature notes enhances their concentration, boosts physical endurance, and alleviates academic stress. Moreover, instructors and educators emphasize brave photographer as a core pillar of personal development and fair play. Whether practicing on sports grounds or exploring international landmarks, students acquire practical knowledge that transcends textbooks. Cultivating healthy habits through balanced sports and informative media prepares youths for success in modern society.",
