      "audioScript": "David: Hello Hoa! What programme or sport are you researching for English class?\nHoa: Hi David! I am presenting about New York City - Central Park and Empire State related to New York City.\nDavid: What is the most exciting aspect of this topic?\nHoa: Audiences and participants are fascinated by Empire State Building and love walking on Broadway.\nDavid: How does it inspire young students?\nHoa: It encourages teamwork, expands knowledge of Central Park, and highlights Statue of Liberty.\nDavid: That is brilliant! I look forward to listening to your speech.",
      "clozeText": "Exploring new york city - central park and empire state provides valuable lessons for secondary school students. Whether situated in New York City or on international screens, this subject inspires teenagers with Empire State Building. Many students find that walking on Broadway helps them build self-confidence and (23) ________. However, experts advise viewers that they (24) ________ spend too many consecutive hours in front of screens. Instead, balancing television viewing with outdoor physical (25) ________ ensures good health. In addition, learning about Central Park broadens our awareness of the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, approaching entertainment with a smart mindset leads to a (27) ________ lifestyle.",
      "readingText": "New York City - Central Park and Empire State has captured the enthusiastic interest of young audiences who appreciate New York City. Combining informative insights with engaging entertainment, it showcases Empire State Building and provides deep perspectives on Central Park. Many teenagers report that participating in walking on Broadway enhances their concentration, boosts physical endurance, and alleviates academic stress. Moreover, instructors and educators emphasize Statue of Liberty as a core pillar of personal development and fair play. Whether practicing on sports grounds or exploring international landmarks, students acquire practical knowledge that transcends textbooks. Cultivating healthy habits through balanced sports and informative media prepares youths for success in modern society.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nExploring new york city - central park and empire state provides valuable lessons for secondary school students. Whether situated in New York City or on international screens, this subject inspires teenagers with Empire State Building. Many students find that walking on Broadway helps them build self-confidence and (23) ________. However, experts advise viewers that they (24) ________ spend too many consecutive hours in front of screens. Instead, balancing television viewing with outdoor physical (25) ________ ensures good health. In addition, learning about Central Park broadens our awareness of the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, approaching entertainment with a smart mindset leads to a (27) ________ lifestyle.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nNew York City - Central Park and Empire State has captured the enthusiastic interest of young audiences who appreciate New York City. Combining informative insights with engaging entertainment, it showcases Empire State Building and provides deep perspectives on Central Park. Many teenagers report that participating in walking on Broadway enhances their concentration, boosts physical endurance, and alleviates academic stress. Moreover, instructors and educators emphasize Statue of Liberty as a core pillar of personal development and fair play. Whether practicing on sports grounds or exploring international landmarks, students acquire practical knowledge that transcends textbooks. Cultivating healthy habits through balanced sports and informative media prepares youths for success in modern society.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Why you like it; Important features of New York City; What benefits it brings; How it helps your study.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, New York City - Central Park and Empire State is an inspiring aspect of modern life. It connects us with New York City while promoting Empire State Building. Engaging in walking on Broadway helps students relieve academic stress and develop Central Park. Furthermore, respecting the spirit of Statue of Liberty encourages discipline and fair play. I believe every student should embrace these healthy habits.",
