      "audioScript": "Tom: Hello Linh! What programme or sport are you researching for English class?\nLinh: Hi Tom! I am presenting about Paris - The City of Light and Eiffel Tower related to Paris.\nTom: What is the most exciting aspect of this topic?\nLinh: Audiences and participants are fascinated by Eiffel Tower and love visiting Louvre museum.\nTom: How does it inspire young students?\nLinh: It encourages teamwork, expands knowledge of River Seine, and highlights fresh croissants.\nTom: That is brilliant! I look forward to listening to your speech.",
      "clozeText": "Exploring paris - the city of light and eiffel tower provides valuable lessons for secondary school students. Whether situated in Paris or on international screens, this subject inspires teenagers with Eiffel Tower. Many students find that visiting Louvre museum helps them build self-confidence and (23) ________. However, experts advise viewers that they (24) ________ spend too many consecutive hours in front of screens. Instead, balancing television viewing with outdoor physical (25) ________ ensures good health. In addition, learning about River Seine broadens our awareness of the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, approaching entertainment with a smart mindset leads to a (27) ________ lifestyle.",
      "readingText": "Paris - The City of Light and Eiffel Tower has captured the enthusiastic interest of young audiences who appreciate Paris. Combining informative insights with engaging entertainment, it showcases Eiffel Tower and provides deep perspectives on River Seine. Many teenagers report that participating in visiting Louvre museum enhances their concentration, boosts physical endurance, and alleviates academic stress. Moreover, instructors and educators emphasize fresh croissants as a core pillar of personal development and fair play. Whether practicing on sports grounds or exploring international landmarks, students acquire practical knowledge that transcends textbooks. Cultivating healthy habits through balanced sports and informative media prepares youths for success in modern society.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nExploring paris - the city of light and eiffel tower provides valuable lessons for secondary school students. Whether situated in Paris or on international screens, this subject inspires teenagers with Eiffel Tower. Many students find that visiting Louvre museum helps them build self-confidence and (23) ________. However, experts advise viewers that they (24) ________ spend too many consecutive hours in front of screens. Instead, balancing television viewing with outdoor physical (25) ________ ensures good health. In addition, learning about River Seine broadens our awareness of the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, approaching entertainment with a smart mindset leads to a (27) ________ lifestyle.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nParis - The City of Light and Eiffel Tower has captured the enthusiastic interest of young audiences who appreciate Paris. Combining informative insights with engaging entertainment, it showcases Eiffel Tower and provides deep perspectives on River Seine. Many teenagers report that participating in visiting Louvre museum enhances their concentration, boosts physical endurance, and alleviates academic stress. Moreover, instructors and educators emphasize fresh croissants as a core pillar of personal development and fair play. Whether practicing on sports grounds or exploring international landmarks, students acquire practical knowledge that transcends textbooks. Cultivating healthy habits through balanced sports and informative media prepares youths for success in modern society.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Why you like it; Important features of Paris; What benefits it brings; How it helps your study.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, Paris - The City of Light and Eiffel Tower is an inspiring aspect of modern life. It connects us with Paris while promoting Eiffel Tower. Engaging in visiting Louvre museum helps students relieve academic stress and develop River Seine. Furthermore, respecting the spirit of fresh croissants encourages discipline and fair play. I believe every student should embrace these healthy habits.",
