      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_8_gk2.mp3",
      "audioScript": "David: Hi Hoa! What environmental, shopping, or disaster response issue are you reviewing?\nHoa: Hi David! I am presenting about Reforestation and Protecting Wildlife in Cuc Phuong National Park at Cuc Phuong rainforest.\nDavid: What is the most critical aspect of this situation?\nHoa: Experts and citizens are paying close attention to ancient Thousand-Year Banyan trees and promoting planting native tree saplings.\nDavid: How does it safeguard human communities or foster sustainability?\nHoa: It mitigates endangered Delacour langurs and emphasizes the vital function of forest ranger patrol.\nDavid: Outstanding! This presentation addresses urgent real-world challenges.",
      "clozeText": "Protecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In Cuc Phuong rainforest, stakeholders are addressing ancient Thousand-Year Banyan trees to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in planting native tree saplings, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and forest ranger patrol guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Reforestation and Protecting Wildlife in Cuc Phuong National Park addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing Cuc Phuong rainforest. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified ancient Thousand-Year Banyan trees, necessitating urgent action on endangered Delacour langurs. Citizens and volunteers who commit to planting native tree saplings have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on forest ranger patrol to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nProtecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In Cuc Phuong rainforest, stakeholders are addressing ancient Thousand-Year Banyan trees to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in planting native tree saplings, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and forest ranger patrol guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nReforestation and Protecting Wildlife in Cuc Phuong National Park addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing Cuc Phuong rainforest. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified ancient Thousand-Year Banyan trees, necessitating urgent action on endangered Delacour langurs. Citizens and volunteers who commit to planting native tree saplings have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on forest ranger patrol to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Problem in Cuc Phuong rainforest; Key factors like ancient Thousand-Year Banyan trees; Recommended actions like planting native tree saplings; Importance of forest ranger patrol.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my perspective, Reforestation and Protecting Wildlife in Cuc Phuong National Park highlights critical challenges that demand immediate public attention. In Cuc Phuong rainforest, the consequences of ancient Thousand-Year Banyan trees underline the necessity of environmental vigilance. By actively taking part in planting native tree saplings, citizens can alleviate ecological strain and protect vulnerable areas. Furthermore, supporting forest ranger patrol ensures that our communities remain resilient against natural hazards. Together, we can build a secure and sustainable future.",
