      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_8_gk2.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Tom: Hi Linh! What environmental, shopping, or disaster response issue are you reviewing?\nLinh: Hi Tom! I am presenting about Flea Markets and Second-Hand Clothing Thrift Culture at weekend flea market.\nTom: What is the most critical aspect of this situation?\nLinh: Experts and citizens are paying close attention to vintage denim jackets and promoting swapping pre-loved garments.\nTom: How does it safeguard human communities or foster sustainability?\nLinh: It mitigates affordable upcycled clothing and emphasizes the vital function of circular fashion workshop.\nTom: Outstanding! This presentation addresses urgent real-world challenges.",
      "clozeText": "Protecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In weekend flea market, stakeholders are addressing vintage denim jackets to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in swapping pre-loved garments, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and circular fashion workshop guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Flea Markets and Second-Hand Clothing Thrift Culture addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing weekend flea market. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified vintage denim jackets, necessitating urgent action on affordable upcycled clothing. Citizens and volunteers who commit to swapping pre-loved garments have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on circular fashion workshop to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nProtecting our natural environment and responding effectively to natural hazards are critical civic responsibilities. In weekend flea market, stakeholders are addressing vintage denim jackets to safeguard local ecosystems and (23) ________. When consumers engage in swapping pre-loved garments, they reduce unnecessary waste and support sustainable (24) ________. Meanwhile, during severe weather events, residents (25) ________ follow official emergency evacuation instructions. Modern technology, such as early warning sensors, helps communities minimize the destruction caused by natural (26) ________. In conclusion, proactive collaboration and circular fashion workshop guarantee a safer, more resilient (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nFlea Markets and Second-Hand Clothing Thrift Culture addresses one of the most pressing environmental and socioeconomic challenges facing weekend flea market. Over recent years, rapid urbanization and climate variations have intensified vintage denim jackets, necessitating urgent action on affordable upcycled clothing. Citizens and volunteers who commit to swapping pre-loved garments have demonstrated that grassroots initiatives can yield tangible ecological benefits. Furthermore, emergency responders and urban planners rely heavily on circular fashion workshop to prevent casualties and maintain civic order. Whether making conscious ethical retail choices or strengthening infrastructure against natural perils, public awareness remains paramount. By combining responsible environmental stewardship with scientific hazard preparedness, communities construct a resilient foundation.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Problem in weekend flea market; Key factors like vintage denim jackets; Recommended actions like swapping pre-loved garments; Importance of circular fashion workshop.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my perspective, Flea Markets and Second-Hand Clothing Thrift Culture highlights critical challenges that demand immediate public attention. In weekend flea market, the consequences of vintage denim jackets underline the necessity of environmental vigilance. By actively taking part in swapping pre-loved garments, citizens can alleviate ecological strain and protect vulnerable areas. Furthermore, supporting circular fashion workshop ensures that our communities remain resilient against natural hazards. Together, we can build a secure and sustainable future.",
