      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_9_gk2.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Tom: Hi Linh! What topic on gastronomy, tourism, or global linguistics are you presenting?\nLinh: Hi Tom! I am presenting about Sustainable Community Homestays in Sapa Highlands at Ta Van ethnic hamlet.\nTom: What is the most fascinating aspect of this subject?\nLinh: Audiences and experts are intrigued by panoramic terraced mountain views and eager to practice staying with Giay families.\nTom: How does it broaden our culinary knowledge or cultural horizons?\nLinh: It showcases traditional wood-fired herbal baths and highlights the significance of woven bamboo backpack.\nTom: Brilliant! That will stimulate great discussions in our English classroom.",
      "clozeText": "Exploring international cuisines, eco-friendly tourism, and linguistic diversity enriches our teenage perspectives. In Ta Van ethnic hamlet, culinary masters and linguists emphasize panoramic terraced mountain views as an essential element of cultural (23) ________. When travelers embrace staying with Giay families, they promote environmental conservation and support local (24) ________. If someone wants to become a fluent international communicator, they (25) ________ master diverse dialects of English. Furthermore, understanding traditional wood-fired herbal baths helps people appreciate foreign traditions without losing their own cultural (26) ________. In summary, respecting woven bamboo backpack paves the way for genuine global understanding and mutual (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Sustainable Community Homestays in Sapa Highlands represents an intriguing facet of modern globalization, culinary refinement, and cross-cultural exchange in Ta Van ethnic hamlet. Whether preparing delicate regional dishes or examining phonetic nuances, this subject combines panoramic terraced mountain views with traditional wood-fired herbal baths. Travelers and researchers who practice staying with Giay families gain deep appreciation for the social customs that nurture human connection. Hospitality experts and educators highlight woven bamboo backpack as a benchmark for sustainable cultural preservation and ethical tourism. Moreover, mastering English as a global language equips Vietnamese teenagers to share our nation's wonders with foreign audiences. By harmonizing local gastronomy, ecological responsibility, and linguistic proficiency, students step confidently onto the global stage.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nExploring international cuisines, eco-friendly tourism, and linguistic diversity enriches our teenage perspectives. In Ta Van ethnic hamlet, culinary masters and linguists emphasize panoramic terraced mountain views as an essential element of cultural (23) ________. When travelers embrace staying with Giay families, they promote environmental conservation and support local (24) ________. If someone wants to become a fluent international communicator, they (25) ________ master diverse dialects of English. Furthermore, understanding traditional wood-fired herbal baths helps people appreciate foreign traditions without losing their own cultural (26) ________. In summary, respecting woven bamboo backpack paves the way for genuine global understanding and mutual (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nSustainable Community Homestays in Sapa Highlands represents an intriguing facet of modern globalization, culinary refinement, and cross-cultural exchange in Ta Van ethnic hamlet. Whether preparing delicate regional dishes or examining phonetic nuances, this subject combines panoramic terraced mountain views with traditional wood-fired herbal baths. Travelers and researchers who practice staying with Giay families gain deep appreciation for the social customs that nurture human connection. Hospitality experts and educators highlight woven bamboo backpack as a benchmark for sustainable cultural preservation and ethical tourism. Moreover, mastering English as a global language equips Vietnamese teenagers to share our nation's wonders with foreign audiences. By harmonizing local gastronomy, ecological responsibility, and linguistic proficiency, students step confidently onto the global stage.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Setting in Ta Van ethnic hamlet; Key factors like panoramic terraced mountain views; Recommended practices like staying with Giay families; Role of woven bamboo backpack.",
