      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_9_gk2.mp3",
      "audioScript": "David: Hi Hoa! What topic on gastronomy, tourism, or global linguistics are you presenting?\nHoa: Hi David! I am presenting about Varieties of World Englishes: British versus American Idioms at linguistics lecture hall.\nDavid: What is the most fascinating aspect of this subject?\nHoa: Audiences and experts are intrigued by distinct phonetic intonations and eager to practice comparing colloquial idioms.\nDavid: How does it broaden our culinary knowledge or cultural horizons?\nHoa: It showcases divergent everyday vocabulary and highlights the significance of bilingual dialect dictionary.\nDavid: Brilliant! That will stimulate great discussions in our English classroom.",
      "clozeText": "Exploring international cuisines, eco-friendly tourism, and linguistic diversity enriches our teenage perspectives. In linguistics lecture hall, culinary masters and linguists emphasize distinct phonetic intonations as an essential element of cultural (23) ________. When travelers embrace comparing colloquial idioms, they promote environmental conservation and support local (24) ________. If someone wants to become a fluent international communicator, they (25) ________ master diverse dialects of English. Furthermore, understanding divergent everyday vocabulary helps people appreciate foreign traditions without losing their own cultural (26) ________. In summary, respecting bilingual dialect dictionary paves the way for genuine global understanding and mutual (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Varieties of World Englishes: British versus American Idioms represents an intriguing facet of modern globalization, culinary refinement, and cross-cultural exchange in linguistics lecture hall. Whether preparing delicate regional dishes or examining phonetic nuances, this subject combines distinct phonetic intonations with divergent everyday vocabulary. Travelers and researchers who practice comparing colloquial idioms gain deep appreciation for the social customs that nurture human connection. Hospitality experts and educators highlight bilingual dialect dictionary as a benchmark for sustainable cultural preservation and ethical tourism. Moreover, mastering English as a global language equips Vietnamese teenagers to share our nation's wonders with foreign audiences. By harmonizing local gastronomy, ecological responsibility, and linguistic proficiency, students step confidently onto the global stage.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nExploring international cuisines, eco-friendly tourism, and linguistic diversity enriches our teenage perspectives. In linguistics lecture hall, culinary masters and linguists emphasize distinct phonetic intonations as an essential element of cultural (23) ________. When travelers embrace comparing colloquial idioms, they promote environmental conservation and support local (24) ________. If someone wants to become a fluent international communicator, they (25) ________ master diverse dialects of English. Furthermore, understanding divergent everyday vocabulary helps people appreciate foreign traditions without losing their own cultural (26) ________. In summary, respecting bilingual dialect dictionary paves the way for genuine global understanding and mutual (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nVarieties of World Englishes: British versus American Idioms represents an intriguing facet of modern globalization, culinary refinement, and cross-cultural exchange in linguistics lecture hall. Whether preparing delicate regional dishes or examining phonetic nuances, this subject combines distinct phonetic intonations with divergent everyday vocabulary. Travelers and researchers who practice comparing colloquial idioms gain deep appreciation for the social customs that nurture human connection. Hospitality experts and educators highlight bilingual dialect dictionary as a benchmark for sustainable cultural preservation and ethical tourism. Moreover, mastering English as a global language equips Vietnamese teenagers to share our nation's wonders with foreign audiences. By harmonizing local gastronomy, ecological responsibility, and linguistic proficiency, students step confidently onto the global stage.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Setting in linguistics lecture hall; Key factors like distinct phonetic intonations; Recommended practices like comparing colloquial idioms; Role of bilingual dialect dictionary.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my view, Varieties of World Englishes: British versus American Idioms represents a wonderful opportunity for cultural appreciation. Located in linguistics lecture hall, it celebrates distinct phonetic intonations and demonstrates how local heritage thrives. Taking part in comparing colloquial idioms enriches our understanding of community values and promotes divergent everyday vocabulary. Furthermore, respecting bilingual dialect dictionary reinforces ethical tourism and international understanding. I look forward to exploring more of these rich cultural traditions.",
