      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_9_gk2.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Tom: Hi Linh! What topic on gastronomy, tourism, or global linguistics are you presenting?\nLinh: Hi Tom! I am presenting about Traditional Vegetarianism (An Chay) in Vietnamese Culture at Buddhist pagoda kitchen.\nTom: What is the most fascinating aspect of this subject?\nLinh: Audiences and experts are intrigued by tofu and mushroom culinary substitutes and eager to practice preparing vegetarian feasts.\nTom: How does it broaden our culinary knowledge or cultural horizons?\nLinh: It showcases mindful compassionate nutrition and highlights the significance of wooden temple gong.\nTom: Brilliant! That will stimulate great discussions in our English classroom.",
      "clozeText": "Exploring international cuisines, eco-friendly tourism, and linguistic diversity enriches our teenage perspectives. In Buddhist pagoda kitchen, culinary masters and linguists emphasize tofu and mushroom culinary substitutes as an essential element of cultural (23) ________. When travelers embrace preparing vegetarian feasts, they promote environmental conservation and support local (24) ________. If someone wants to become a fluent international communicator, they (25) ________ master diverse dialects of English. Furthermore, understanding mindful compassionate nutrition helps people appreciate foreign traditions without losing their own cultural (26) ________. In summary, respecting wooden temple gong paves the way for genuine global understanding and mutual (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Traditional Vegetarianism (An Chay) in Vietnamese Culture represents an intriguing facet of modern globalization, culinary refinement, and cross-cultural exchange in Buddhist pagoda kitchen. Whether preparing delicate regional dishes or examining phonetic nuances, this subject combines tofu and mushroom culinary substitutes with mindful compassionate nutrition. Travelers and researchers who practice preparing vegetarian feasts gain deep appreciation for the social customs that nurture human connection. Hospitality experts and educators highlight wooden temple gong as a benchmark for sustainable cultural preservation and ethical tourism. Moreover, mastering English as a global language equips Vietnamese teenagers to share our nation's wonders with foreign audiences. By harmonizing local gastronomy, ecological responsibility, and linguistic proficiency, students step confidently onto the global stage.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nExploring international cuisines, eco-friendly tourism, and linguistic diversity enriches our teenage perspectives. In Buddhist pagoda kitchen, culinary masters and linguists emphasize tofu and mushroom culinary substitutes as an essential element of cultural (23) ________. When travelers embrace preparing vegetarian feasts, they promote environmental conservation and support local (24) ________. If someone wants to become a fluent international communicator, they (25) ________ master diverse dialects of English. Furthermore, understanding mindful compassionate nutrition helps people appreciate foreign traditions without losing their own cultural (26) ________. In summary, respecting wooden temple gong paves the way for genuine global understanding and mutual (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nTraditional Vegetarianism (An Chay) in Vietnamese Culture represents an intriguing facet of modern globalization, culinary refinement, and cross-cultural exchange in Buddhist pagoda kitchen. Whether preparing delicate regional dishes or examining phonetic nuances, this subject combines tofu and mushroom culinary substitutes with mindful compassionate nutrition. Travelers and researchers who practice preparing vegetarian feasts gain deep appreciation for the social customs that nurture human connection. Hospitality experts and educators highlight wooden temple gong as a benchmark for sustainable cultural preservation and ethical tourism. Moreover, mastering English as a global language equips Vietnamese teenagers to share our nation's wonders with foreign audiences. By harmonizing local gastronomy, ecological responsibility, and linguistic proficiency, students step confidently onto the global stage.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Mention: Setting in Buddhist pagoda kitchen; Key factors like tofu and mushroom culinary substitutes; Recommended practices like preparing vegetarian feasts; Role of wooden temple gong.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my view, Traditional Vegetarianism (An Chay) in Vietnamese Culture represents a wonderful opportunity for cultural appreciation. Located in Buddhist pagoda kitchen, it celebrates tofu and mushroom culinary substitutes and demonstrates how local heritage thrives. Taking part in preparing vegetarian feasts enriches our understanding of community values and promotes mindful compassionate nutrition. Furthermore, respecting wooden temple gong reinforces ethical tourism and international understanding. I look forward to exploring more of these rich cultural traditions.",
